 "deviations": [
  "Test-route guard (G-2 \"refuses while any test-route run exists\"): a run is detected by its existence only, a runs/ entry in an output directory of the P4-P6 lines or under matrix/, fig3/, ablation/, replicates/ (Sec. 8.6), or a status record in outputs/framelease_v4/queue_p4; no result file is opened (Sec. 9.11).",
  "Stress tests: the freeze takes one registered report per test (stress_bench.py --registered) and refuses S2 or S3 with a violation (Sec. 7.6: the admitted actions with bound >= D* and the commits violating Eq. 9 \"must be 0\"); S1 has no pass criterion and is recorded as measured.",
  "G-3: the P4-P6 job files, the RL freeze and the test-freeze record are covered by the test freeze's own sha256 manifest, cited in this entry and sealed with it; registration.py is unchanged.",
  "The P2 data manifest is entered in Sec. 13.2 by this entry when no earlier entry cites it (Sec. 5.9: the dataset manifest is entered in Sec. 13 as part of the test freeze).",
  "Arm identity (GAP_AUDIT Sec. 2, \"Recommended labelling\"; Sec. 4.1 names no launcher arm for these arms): fl_bandit and fl_fqi_nolease run through the launcher arm fl_full with the network file of their family, fl_risk through fl_heuristic at its lease point; each such arm is the pair (launcher arm, network file sha256 or envelope sha256), recorded in the job line (protocol_arm), in the output directory (ablation/<arm>/) and in the block spec."
 ],
